+PHYSICAL INTERPRETATION
+The figure and text explicitly state
+U_chi H(F) U_chi^dagger = H(F exp(i chi)), U_chi=exp(i chi N).
+Thus all values of arg(F) are physically unitarily equivalent: the spectrum
+depends on |F|, not arg(F).  Changing arg(F)=arg(q) nevertheless rotates the
+sector geometry when the Bargmann coordinate frame is held fixed.  No claim
+that this rotation changes the spectrum is made.
+
+ROLE OF |q|
+Ray angles use only arg(q).  |q| was fixed at 1 in every panel and was never
+allowed to change ray positions.  Since |s|=sqrt(|q|), changing |q| only
+rescales Re(Delta S)=4 Re(st), hence the strength of exponential dominance.
+The figure represents dominance by restrained sector shading and does not
+misrepresent |q| as an angular effect.
